# [PLAN] Disk hygiene — Plan 3 Phase 1 (María, 2026-08-23)
# Install:  crontab -l > /tmp/c; cat src/scripts/disk-hygiene.crontab >> /tmp/c; crontab /tmp/c
# Weekly report Sundays 03:00; weekly sweep Sundays 03:30 (14-day retention).
0 3 * * 0 LUPIN_ROOT=/mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/src/scripts/disk-hygiene-report.sh >> /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/io/claude_code_hooks/logs/disk-hygiene-report.log 2>&1
30 3 * * 0 LUPIN_ROOT=/mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/src/scripts/sweep-hook-logs.sh --apply >> /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/io/claude_code_hooks/logs/disk-hygiene-sweep.log 2>&1

# io/tmp expiry — row 730b33f2 (Rick's ruling 2026-09-26, María accountable).
#
# DAILY, not weekly, and that is deliberate: retention is 7 days, so a weekly tick
# would let a file reach 14 before its first chance to be swept — "deleted after 7
# days" would mean "deleted somewhere between 7 and 14". Daily makes the worst case
# 8 days instead of 14.
#
# 🔴 19:00, NOT THE SMALL HOURS — THE BOX IS OFF THEN AND THE JOB SIMPLY NEVER RUNS.
# CLAUDE.md § Off-peak scheduling calls ~11 PM–10 AM the dead window, and it is not
# a record of habit. Re-derived 2026-09-26 from `journalctl --list-boots --no-pager`
# (20 boots, 2026-09-04 to 2026-09-26): the LATEST any boot began is 18:12 and the
# EARLIEST any completed boot ended is 20:13, so 19:00 is the one hour inside every
# single boot window in the sample. Nothing in that sample was up at 04:00 — a
# 04:00 entry would have been a job that reports success by never firing, which is
# the same shape of bug as the -mtime off-by-one this row exists to avoid.
#
# @reboot is the catch-up arm: a day the box is off at 19:00 gets swept on the next
# power-on instead of waiting a full extra day. Cheap — a no-op costs one `find`.
#
# ⚠️ --apply IS LOAD-BEARING. Without it the sweep dry-runs forever, printing an
# eligible count and deleting nothing. test_the_crontab_entry_actually_applies
# asserts it is present.
#
# ⚠️ A .crontab FILE IS NOT AN INSTALLED SWEEP. Install with the line at the top of
# this file, then verify with `crontab -l | grep sweep-io-tmp` — and read the WHOLE
# listing, not a `head`-truncated one.
#
# 🔴 THE TWO SUNDAY ENTRIES ABOVE ARE IN THE DEAD WINDOW TOO — 03:00 and 03:30, and
# no boot in the sample was up at either. They are NOT changed here: they are
# María's from 2026-08-23 and moving someone else's scheduled job is her call, not
# this row's. Reported to Mr. Radio 2026-09-26; the guard test carries them in an
# explicit pending-ruling list so a THIRD dead-window entry still reddens.
0 19 * * * LUPIN_ROOT=/mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/src/scripts/sweep-io-tmp.sh --apply >> /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/io/claude_code_hooks/logs/io-tmp-sweep.log 2>&1
@reboot LUPIN_ROOT=/mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/src/scripts/sweep-io-tmp.sh --apply >> /mnt/DATA01/include/www.deepily.ai/projects/lupin/io/claude_code_hooks/logs/io-tmp-sweep.log 2>&1
